<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan FGEP buys 54,000T U.S. corn at tender.</title>
<headline>Taiwan FGEP buys 54,000T U.S. corn at tender.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's FGEP corn-buying group bought a shipment of 54,000 tonnes of U.S. No.2 corn from Mitsui at tender on Wednesday, traders said.</p>
<p>The FGEP group comprises Fwu Sow Grain, Great Wall Enterprise, President Enterprise and Ever Smile Feed Mill Co.  </p>
<p>The shipment was bought on a cost-and-freight basis.</p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follow:</p>
<p>			U.S. Gulf  Pacific N.W.   Price/Future</p>
<p>			Nov 10-25  Nov 26-Dce 9</p>
<p>	    18,000				    US$164.95</p>
<p>	    36,000				    87.48 US Cents/Dec</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
